  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cooperation SMHI-SHS Moldova 2024-2029 - International Development Cooperation-Moldova SMHI-SHS</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Samarbete SMHI-SHS Moldavien 2024-2029</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Moldavien st&#xe5;r inf&#xf6;r flera naturliga faror inklusive &#xf6;versv&#xe4;mningar, torka, jordb&#xe4;vningar, hagelstormar och extrem v&#xe4;rme. Dessa faror utg&#xf6;r utmaningar f&#xf6;r landets jordbrukssektor, infrastruktur och befolkningens allm&#xe4;nna
v&#xe4;lbefinnande.&#xc4;ven om klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringarna f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas &#xf6;ka Moldaviens s&#xe5;rbarhet, m&#xe4;rks dess effekter redan i jordbrukssektorn och landets &#xf6;vergripande f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning. Detta fem&#xe5;riga projekt med en total budget som t&#xe4;cks helt av Sida p&#xe5; 29 990 800 SEK syftar till att &#xf6;ka kapaciteten f&#xf6;r hydrologiska, meteorologiska och klimatologiska informationstj&#xe4;nster vid Serviciul Hidrometeorologic de Stat (SHS) som nationell leverant&#xf6;r av meteorologiska, hydrologiska och klimatdata som samt varningar f&#xf6;r katastrofrisk.
Projektet Strengthening Hydrometeorological Capacity in Moldova (SHC Moldova) syftar till att st&#xf6;dja SHS i att st&#xe4;rka deras datahantering, prognoser och katastrofriskkommunikation med ett starkt fokus p&#xe5; digitalisering och
automatiseringsprocesser.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Moldova faces several natural hazards including flooding, drought, earthquakes, hailstorms, and extreme heat. These hazards pose challenges to the country&#x2019;s agricultural sector, infrastructure, and overall well&#xad;being of the population. While climate change is expected to increase the vulnerability of Moldova, its effects
are already being felt in the agricultural sector and the country&#x2019;s overall livelihood.
This 5 years project with a total budget covered fully by Sida of 29 990 800 SEK aims to enhance the capacity for hydrological, meteorological and climatological information services at Serviciul Hidrometeorologic de Stat (SHS) as the national provider of meteorological, hydrological and climate data as well as disaster risk warnings.
The Strengthening Hydrometeorological Capacity in Moldova (SHC&#xad;Moldova) project aims to support SHS in strengthening their data management, forecasting and disaster risk communication skills with a strong focus on
digitalization and automatization processes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The SHC-Moldova project aims to support SHS in strengthening their data management, forecasting and disaster risk communication skills with a strong focus on digitalization and automatization processes. The project will develop human technical capacity and improve weather and water information services, including forecast and early warning systems, as well as improve disaster risk communication and action. Good governance procedures form an integral part of the capacity development effort.

Project Outcome: 
 - Enhanced capacity for hydrological, meteorological and climatological information services at SHS in its role as national provider of meteorological, hydrological and climate data as well as disaster risk warnings.

&#x2022; Output 1  Strengthened capacity for information technology (IT).
&#x2022; Output 2  Strengthened capacity for management of historical data .
&#x2022; Output 3  Strengthened capacity for meteorological forecasting.
&#x2022; Output 4  Strengthened capacity for hydrological forecasting.
&#x2022; Output 5  Strengthened capacity for early warning services.
&#x2022; Output 6  Strengthened capacity for maintaining a sustainable institution</narrative>
  </description>
